  "prompt": "For each promotion that started in October 2024 (start_date from 1 to 31 October 2024), give the units sold on promotion and the units of its products in the baseline. A sales line is on a promotion when it carries that promotion's ID in order_lines.promo_id, whatever its date; where two promotions overlap on a product, a line carries only the deeper one, so it counts once. The baseline ends the day before the promotion's start_date and has as many days as the promotion ran, start_date and end_date both counted; it holds every sales line of the promotion's products in those days, whatever promotion the line carries. Days are sales.order_date, the UTC day of the order. A promotion with no sale in a period still shows, with 0 for it. Return three columns, in this order: promo_id, promo_units and baseline_units. Return one row for each such promotion. Any row order is fine.",
  "output_contract": {
    "columns": [
      {
        "name": "promo_id",
        "type_class": "numeric"
      },
